{title: Scarborough Fair}
{artist: Tradicionál (Anglie)}
{key: Ami}

{start_of_verse: label="1."}
[Ami]Are you going to [G]Scarborough [Ami]Fair?
[C]Parsley, [Ami]sage, rose[C]mary [D]and [Ami]thyme;
Re[Ami]member me to [C]one who lives [G]there,
[Ami]She once was a [G]true love of [Ami]mine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: label="2."}
[Ami]Tell her to make me a [G]cambric [Ami]shirt,
[C]Parsley, [Ami]sage, rose[C]mary [D]and [Ami]thyme;
With[Ami]out no seams nor [C]needle[G]work,
[Ami]Then she'll be a [G]true love of [Ami]mine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: label="3."}
[Ami]Tell her to wash it in [G]yonder dry [Ami]well,
[C]Parsley, [Ami]sage, rose[C]mary [D]and [Ami]thyme;
Where [Ami]never sprung water, nor [C]rain ever [G]fell,
[Ami]And she shall be a [G]true love of [Ami]mine.
{end_of_verse}
